{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1001", "sample_idx": 6, "model_name": "mistralai/mistral-small-4-119b-2603", "content": "Lo thus doth mine itinerary for thy voyage to Nippon’s fair shores unfold in thy desired tongue:\n\n**First Day**\nWhenas the sun doth rise o’er the eastern sea bringeth thee to the hallowed gates of Tokyo’s great Narita where thou shalt enter the land of the Rising Sun. There take thee the swift train to the city’s heart and there alight at Tokyo Station. Seek forthwith the quarters of Asakusa and pay homage to the sacred Senso-ji where the great Kannon’s spirit doth dwell. Feast upon the delights of street food as the lanterns do glow and retire to thy repose in an inn most humble.\n\n**Second Day**\nWhen morrow’s light doth break set thy course for the imperial grandeur of the Meiji Shrine where the spirits of old Japan do rest. Wander through the vast forest paths and thence to Harajuku where the youth of the land do dance in fanciful attire. In the afternoon make haste to Shibuya’s crossing where the multitudes flow like a river of souls and ascend unto the Shibuya Sky for a prospect most wondrous. As the day waneth dine at a ramen house most famed and rest thy bones.\n\n**Third Day**\nArise betimes and take the train to Nikko where nature’s splendor doth reign supreme. Behold the Toshogu Shrine where gold doth gleam and the sacred cedars whisper ancient tales. Return to Tokyo by eventide and in the night partake in a performance of Kabuki or Noh if fortune doth favor thee.\n\n**Fourth Day**\nUpon the morrow embark upon the Tokaido Shinkansen bound for Kyoto the ancient capital. When thou dost arrive seek the bamboo groves of Arashiyama and lose thyself in their emerald embrace. In the evening wander through the lantern-lit streets of Gion where the geisha do glide like specters of old.\n\n**Fifth Day**\nAwake to the call of the cuckoo and repair to the golden pavilion of Kinkaku-ji its top clad in gilded glory. Then to the Ryoan-ji where the stones do lie in silent meditation. As the sun dips low make thy way to Fushimi Inari and walk the torii gates that climb the sacred mountain. Dine upon unagi most savory and rest.\n\n**Sixth Day**\nWhen dawn doth break take the path to Nara where the deer do bow and the Todai-ji’s great Buddha doth sit in silent judgment. Return to Kyoto by eventide and in the night partake in a tea ceremony most refined.\n\n**Seventh Day**\nRise betimes and take the train to Hiroshima. There seek the Peace Memorial Park and ponder the folly of war. In the evening cross the Seto Ohashi to the isle of Miyajima and behold the torii gate that stands in the sea. Return to Hiroshima and rest.\n\n**Eighth Day**\nWhen morning cometh take the Shinkansen to Osaka. There ascend the great Osaka Castle and feast upon okonomiyaki in Dotonbori’s bustling streets. As the stars do appear take thy leave of this city of merchants and revelers.\n\n**Ninth Day**\nUpon the ninth day return to Tokyo and in the final hours seek the gardens of the Imperial Palace and the quietude of the East Gardens. In the evening take a last look upon the city from the heights of the Tokyo Metropolitan Government Building.\n\n**Tenth Day**\nWhen the tenth morn doth dawn make ready thy departure from this land of wonders and return unto thy own shores with memories most dear.\n\nThus ends thy journey in Nippon’s embrace and may the gods of travel smile upon thy path.", "logprobs": [{"token": "Lo", "logprob": -1.1275019645690918}, {"token": " thus", "logprob": -1.4427415132522583}, {"token": " d", "logprob": -0.20660947263240814}, {"token": "oth", "logprob": -2.3841830625315197e-06}, {"token": " mine", "logprob": -0.3317168354988098}, {"token": " itiner", "logprob": -0.9936856627464294}, {"token": "ary", "logprob": -0.0012753218179568648}, {"token": " for", "logprob": -0.433417946100235}, {"token": " thy", "logprob": -0.06503264605998993}, {"token": " voyage", "logprob": -0.33382490277290344}, {"token": " to", "logpr